{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hypergraph"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" Edge position ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is incidence number ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index order, and within a hyperedge in ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"until its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array must be rebuilt for it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The LabeledGraph law."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"text":" shifted by n, and of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"text":" it is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"text":". So ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traversal"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Connectivity"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPaths"},{"text":" and the rest run on the view without hashing a vertex. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidentIndexRows"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes the view’s rows out once per call from the base’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidenceRows"},{"text":", in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(n + m + p), so whole-graph algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices) run at an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"adjacency-list copy’s speed on every base.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a range, O(1). On ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which stores its incidences,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every read is O(1) plus the row. On any other base, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"binary-search the hyperedge and find the member by its rank (","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" finds its place in each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over them on a base without a faster ","type":"text"},{"code":"_memberRank","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraph, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the bipartite structure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the view’s components restricted to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"type":"text","text":" are the hypergraph’s."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"]}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdgeIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Neighbors"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/init(base:)"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/base","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeCount","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edgeIndexBound","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/edges-swift.property","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexCount","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertexIndexBound","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/vertices"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instan